WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.560
If you want to know how Tim Curry’s Pennywise
from the 1990 TV mini-series IT is hidden

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.520
in this trailer, then stick around to the
end of this video.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.570
The trailer opens with an overhead shot of
the town.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:17.689
This same angle is also seen in 1989 during
the first movie.

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:20.200
Here are the two side by side for comparison.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.010
We then see the missing posters that are piling
up once again.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.700
The town is decorated with balloons in the
background, possibly for the Derry Canal Days

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.210
festival, which the carnival and celebration
where It makes a return in the book.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.580
We can’t see the movie theater marquee,
but in the first movie, the titles were accurate

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.960
to the time period, so maybe in this movie
it’ll be showing 10 Cloverfield Lane, Don’t

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.990
Breathe, Lights Out…

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.720
UGH WHAT A GOOD YEAR.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.010
In the next scene we see someone drowning
in the sewers.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.350
The first time he comes up from the water
he sees nothing.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:49.120
The second time there’s blood in the water,
and the third time there’s a good old friend

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.780
who just woke up from his nappy nap and probably
wants to play.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.360
Jade of the Orient is the same Chinese restaurant
that the Losers Club has their reunion lunch

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.360
at in the book.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.340
You see the words “try me” on this drink
of the month advertisement.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.830
Is this a coincidence or is this Pennywise
saying “try me”.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.390
Challenge me and see what happens.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.970
In the book, Pennywise does manipulate the
dishes served at the lunch, and leaves similar

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.650
messages throughout the novel, so I think
it’s a possibility.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.010
This shot of Beverly is brief, but you’ll
notice the tall buildings, rain, a police

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.490
car and the fact that she’s not wearing
makeup as she does in her other appearances.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.940
I think this is her late night escape from
her abusive husband Tom Rogan.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.790
The two live together in Chicago at the start
of Chapter 2 and Beverly didn’t have much

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.810
time to grab anything as she escaped.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.840
Everyone is rushing to get inside, but she’s
focused on getting away from her abusive husband.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.230
Like I mentioned earlier, I think this carnival
is part of the Derry Canal Days Festival,

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.470
and one room in the funhouse contains a series
of swinging clown pendulums.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.710
Some of these look just like Tim Curry’s
Pennywise from the 1990 adaptation of IT,

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.750
it has the yellow clown suit, orange pom-pom
buttons and red tufts of hair, there’s a

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.920
similar reference in the first movie where
Curry’s Pennywise can be seen in the room

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.290
full of clown statues.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.440
This funhouse scene isn’t in the book, but
there is a scene where Bill encounters a kid

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.590
on a skateboard and Bill warns him not to
play around the sewers.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.670
Then Bill gets this urge to ride the skateboard
because the inner child inside of him is essentially

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:02.729
re-emerging.

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:06.680
So I think instead of the skateboard, Bill
relives his childhood by going into the funhouse

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.869
maze and instead of him warning the kid, he
maybe saves the kid while he’s is in actual

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:11.869
danger.

00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:15.400
Also, can I just point out this is the second
horror movie this year to have a mirror maze?

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.920
"WHAT IF I'M A MONST--"

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.220
"ASKJFLSDFJKL"

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.680
Bill crashes into this glass that seems to
be right in front of him.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.640
Does It maybe have the ability to change the
layout of the maze to drive Bill crazy?

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.480
If so, it could make for some great psychological
horror.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.610
When Pennywise is revealed, the tongue is
hanging out further than we’ve ever seen

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.950
it, like some kind of weird smartphone filter.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.020
I think this is to show that IT is preparing
for a meal because it senses fear, and feeds

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:38.940
off of fear.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.640
"I'll take all of you...

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:47.819
I'll feast on your flesh as I feed on your
fear..."

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:51.880
We saw this a lot with all the drool in the
first movie, and I think this tongue shot

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.750
is essentially taking that to the next level.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.080
When the Losers show up at the house on 29
Neibolt St, Eddie has a bloody gauze on his cheek

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.060
similar to where Beverly has one as a kid;
Mike seems to have wrap around his wrist,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:06.209
maybe a second coming of Eddie having the
cast in the first one, and Bill is missing

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:07.319
from the group.

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:10.849
Maybe he tries going in by himself and the
others have to come save him?

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:14.930
In this next scene, a red balloon floats by
this facility and seems to drive the inmates

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:15.930
crazy.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.370
This guy has the initials J.H.P.H on his back.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.370
The facility that Henry Bowers is kept in
during the 27 year gap in the book is called

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.349
Juniper Hill Mental Asylum, so I think for
the movie it’s been renamed to Juniper Hill

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.930
Psychiatric Hospital.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.379
Maybe Henry isn’t the only mental case that
It gets on It’s side side this time.

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:33.099
Also, these guys look like they’re at a
metal concert.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:35.620
"IT's coming back around every 27 years!"

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:40.069
These are the same three doors the Losers
Club encounters inside 29 Neibolt Street in

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.660
the first movie, but one cool detail I noticed
is that the blood is trickling up rather than

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.900
down, just as Pennywise is rising again, or
perhaps “floating” back to the surface.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.380
Now in the book there’s a chapter called
Walking Tours where the Losers go back to

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.410
revisit locations that were important to them
in their childhood.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:59.210
Richie goes back to City Center where he first
encountered It, Beverly goes to where her

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.910
parents’ house was, and Bill goes downtown.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.020
Maybe in the movie though, Bill goes back
to his childhome home as well.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.090
In this shot we what looks to be some kind
of dream or hallucination with Child Bill

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.910
and Adult Bill side by side in the flooded
basement.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:15.660
Either that, or this is some kind of 27 year
challenge on social media.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.569
In the first trailer, there’s a shot of
someone splashing around in blood, and in

00:04:18.569 --> 00:04:22.330
this one, we see that it’s actually Beverly
revisiting the old elementary school bathroom

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.900
where she was bullied as a child.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.800
The graffiti “H*TE CLOWN” has been crossed
out, but it’s unclear what it says under

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.800
that.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.990
Other graffiti includes Greta Keane is a B*tch.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.949
Greta Keane is the movie reimagining of a
character named Greta Bowie from the book

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:38.219
-- in the movie she’s also the daughter
of Norbert Keane, the pharmacist who tries

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.099
to warn Eddie that his aspirator is a gazebo.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.340
"You know what these are?

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:45.650
They're gazebos!!

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.960
They're bull***t!!"

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.139
This small text right here says Beverly Marsh
gets around -- which references the rumor

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:53.490
spread by Greta and her friends that Beverly
is this big sl*t.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.339
Stop censoring me YouTube godd***it!

00:04:55.339 --> 00:05:00.051
There’s also a good look at the bruising
on Beverly’s arm where her husband most

00:05:00.051 --> 00:05:01.139
likely grabbed her during her escape.

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:04.319
Here’s another quick Pennywise appearance
in what I’d assume is Beverly trying to

00:05:04.319 --> 00:05:05.839
break them out of 29 Neibolt Street.

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:08.559
And then if you pause near the end of the
trailer, you’ll get the only look we have

00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:12.619
so far at one of the other forms of It, it
looks like some kind of Zombie-like creature

00:05:12.619 --> 00:05:13.619
that can swim.

00:05:13.619 --> 00:05:18.279
Can’t wait to see what that is, maybe it’s
like an undead version of Bev’s father.

00:05:18.279 --> 00:05:21.059
Here we have one somebody falling down the
well and into this light.

00:05:21.059 --> 00:05:25.009
The true form of It is something called The
Deadlights, which are teased at a couple of

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:26.009
times.

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:28.759
Maybe what we’re seeing here is similar
to what happened to Henry Bowers when he was

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:30.479
pushed into the well by Mike.

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:33.930
For more on that, watch my full video on my
three theories for It: Chapter 2.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.060
Or maybe this is Bill or Richie entering the
Macroverse -- I won’t put any spoilers in

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.809
this video, but fans of the book will know
what I’m talking about.

00:05:40.809 --> 00:05:44.289
One of our last shots Pennywise shutting this
door back up to the surface.

00:05:44.289 --> 00:05:47.360
The only thing this reminds me of is this
one scene from the mini-series that isn’t

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.060
in 
the book.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:54.320
"Take your pick.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.780
B-b-b-billy boy!"

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.490
Be sure to let me know what else you noticed
in the trailer, and click the video on the

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.230
left to see my analysis on the other trailer
for It Chapter 2.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.330
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld, I’ve
got a load of content planned leading up to

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.260
the next movie, and I’ll see you in the
next one.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.720
Assuming we both survive.

